#### Issue #2970: [Bug]: Composio SDK Slow Initialization

### SDK Language

TypeScript / Node.js SDK (`@composio/core`)

### SDK Version

@composio/core@0.6.5

### Runtime Environment

Node 22 on Vercel

### Environment

Vercel / Serverless Function

### Describe the Bug

`@composio/core` adds **~3.9s of blocking latency** on every cold initialization due to two outbound HTTP requests that run during SDK setup:

1. **`GET registry.npmjs.org/@composio/core/latest`** (~3.78s) — version/update check
2. **`POST telemetry.composio.dev/v1/metrics/ingest`** (~3.91s) — telemetry beacon

These requests fire synchronously during `new Composio()` or the first `.create()` call, blocking the entire request pipeline before any actual work (tool loading, LLM calls) can begin.
Even on hot requests the two blocking calls still add **~2.7s** of overhead. There is no caching — every request pays the full penalty.


## Background:

In our Next.js app (Vercel-hosted), we use Composio's Tool Router to provide agent tools via MCP. The initialization overhead adds **3-4 seconds** to every agent chat response — roughly **40% of total request time** (10s).


