#### Issue #13019: Feature Request: Pre-compaction warning event for agents

Feature Request: Pre-compaction warning event for agents
Summary
Inject a system event when context usage reaches a configurable threshold (e.g., 80-90%) so agents can take action before compaction occurs.

Problem
When compaction triggers, the agent loses conversational context with no advance warning. There's no opportunity to:

Save working context to persistent files
Flush conversation logs
Summarize current task state
Preserve critical details that compaction may discard
The new compaction divider (2026.2.9, #11341) helps users see when compaction occurred, but agents receive no signal before or during the event.

Proposed Solution
Inject a system event (similar to heartbeat or reminder events) when context usage crosses a configurable threshold. For example:

[SYSTEM] Context at 85% capacity. Compaction imminent. Save any critical context now.
Configuration
{
  "agents": {
    "defaults": {
      "compaction": {
        "mode": "safeguard",
        "warningThreshold": 0.85
      }
    }
  }
}
Agent behavior
When agents receive this event, they can:

Write working state to memory files
Append conversation logs
Create a brief summary of current task/context
Acknowledge readiness for compaction
Why this matters
Agents that maintain persistent memory (daily logs, conversation files, long-term memory) need a chance to flush state before it's lost. Currently, the only workaround is frequent periodic saves (wasteful) or accepting data loss (unreliable).

This is especially important for:

Long-running technical sessions with accumulated context
Agents with conversation logging rules
Multi-step tasks where losing context means restarting work
Environment
OpenClaw 2026.2.9
Related: #12283 (post-compaction amnesia fix), #11341 (compaction divider)

